sentences.l:
The Master said: “I hand on and do not originate;
I trust antiquity and love it;
I presume to liken myself to our Old Peng.”

The Master said to Yan Yuan: “Put to use, then go forward;
left unused, then withdraw —
only I and you have this!”

The Master said: “Why did you not say:
as for the kind of man he is —
roused to effort, he forgets to eat;
taking joy in it, he forgets his cares;
he does not know old age is about to come — just so.”

The Master said: “I am not one who knew it from birth;
I am one who loves antiquity
and presses eagerly to seek it.”

With nothing, yet playing at having;
empty, yet playing at full;
pinched, yet playing at plenty —
hard indeed to have constancy!

Huxiang was hard to talk with;
a boy was presented,
and the disciples were perplexed.

The Master said: “Approve his coming forward;
do not approve his going back —
why go to such lengths?
A man purifies himself to come forward:
approve his purity;
do not answer for his past.”

The Master said: “In letters, perhaps I am about like others;
living out the gentleman in my own person —
that I have not yet attained.”
